          "_customHTML": "<section data-bs-version=\"5.1\" class=\"content5\" group=\"Content\">\n    <mbr-parameters>\n        <header>Size</header>\n        <input type=\"checkbox\" title=\"Full Width\" name=\"fullWidth\">\n        <input type=\"range\" inline title=\"Top\" name=\"paddingTop\" min=\"0\" max=\"10\" step=\"1\" value=\"5\">\n        <input type=\"range\" inline title=\"Bottom\" name=\"paddingBottom\" min=\"0\" max=\"10\" step=\"1\" value=\"0\">\n        <input type=\"range\" name=\"textWidth\" title=\"Width\" min=\"4\" max=\"12\" value=\"10\" step=\"1\">\n        <header>Show/Hide</header>\n        <input type=\"checkbox\" title=\"Title\" name=\"showTitle\">\n        <input type=\"checkbox\" title=\"Subtitle\" name=\"showSubtitle\" checked>\n        <header>Background</header>\n        <input type=\"color\" title=\"Color\" name=\"bgColor\" value=\"#ffffff\">\n    </mbr-parameters>\n    <div mbr-class=\"{'container': !fullWidth, 'container-fluid': fullWidth}\">\n        <div class=\"row justify-content-center\">\n            <div class=\"col-md-12 col-lg-{{textWidth}}\">\n                <h3 class=\"mbr-section-title mbr-fonts-style mb-4\" mbr-if=\"showTitle\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-section-title\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-2\">\n                    <b>Article Title</b>\n                </h3>\n                <h4 class=\"mbr-section-subtitle mbr-fonts-style mb-4\" mbr-if=\"showSubtitle\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-section-subtitle\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\">8. Dual Navigation Systems</h4>\n                <p class=\"mbr-text mbr-fonts-style\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-text\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-7\">The architecture supports two independent navigation graphs.<br><br><b>Pedestrian Graph</b><br>Nodes: workspace.Waypoints.<br>Used By: All NPC citizens.<br>Purpose: Sidewalks, crosswalks, and building interiors.<br><br><b>Vehicle Graph</b><br>Nodes: workspace.Carpoints.<br>Used By: Cars, buses, and emergency vehicles.<br>Purpose: Road networks with traffic rules.<br><br>Both graphs use the same Dijkstra module but operate on separate adjacency lists. This prevents pedestrians from routing through highways and vehicles from routing through parks.<br><br><b>Why This Is a Good Method:</b><br><br><b>Scalable Architecture<br></b>The three layer separation between scheduling, navigation, and activities allows new locations, schedules, and behaviors to be added without modifying the core systems.<br><br><b>Emergent Behavior from Simple Rules<br></b>Queues form naturally, rush hour congestion appears at intersections, and apartments feel lived in. These behaviors emerge from occupancy locks and schedule data rather than scripted sequences.<br><br><b>Custom Pathfinding</b><br>The system demonstrates the ability to implement graph algorithms from scratch instead of relying exclusively on built in engine features.<br><br><b>Robustness Engineering</b><br>Stuck detection, sit state recovery, traffic light integration, and interruption handling demonstrate consideration of practical edge cases.<br><br><b>Data Driven Design</b><br>NPC behavior is defined by schedule tables and waypoint graphs rather than hardcoded logic. Designers can create new citizen routines by modifying data.<br><br><b>Resource Management</b><br>The occupancy lock pattern provides a straightforward way to manage resource contention between multiple agents. Careful handling of resource acquisition and release is necessary to prevent deadlocks.<br></p>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>",
